{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_30_codex_efficiency_fixes_design", "label": "Codex Efficiency Fixes - Design", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-30-codex-efficiency-fixes-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_30_codex_efficiency_fixes_design_t1_worker_review_prohibition", "label": "T1: SDD worker-review prohibition", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "9/9 depth-2 spawns across 4 corpora were implementer-issued reviewer subagents, all duplicates of the review the controller dispatches anyway; the dispatch contract never says review is not the worker's job, and 'self-review' in the implementer prompt gets reified into a reviewer subagent on harnesses where children can spawn (Codex). Fix: explicit 'you do not dispatch subagents' clause plus a Red Flags row, graded by score_e6.py/score_e5.py against baseline 9/9 worker-issued.", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-30-codex-efficiency-fixes-design.md", "source_location": "## The five treatments / ### T1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_30_codex_efficiency_fixes_design_t2_event_driven_waiting", "label": "T2: Event-driven waiting", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "60-78% of wait_agent calls time out in every corpus (dev 67.1%, spinout 60.2%); source recon shows V2 waits are event subscriptions, not polls - one long wait has the same wake latency as a 10s poll at ~1/90th the calls, and a completed child's FINAL_ANSWER is pushed into the parent's mailbox. Fix: never short-timeout poll; when idle issue ONE wait_agent with timeout_ms 900000+; criterion timeout rate < 25%.", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-30-codex-efficiency-fixes-design.md", "source_location": "## The five treatments / ### T2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_30_codex_efficiency_fixes_design_t3_codex_tools_corrections", "label": "T3: codex-tools.md corrections", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Five claims in the current guidance are contradicted by the Codex source (all file:line-cited): close_agent does not exist in multi-agent V2 (V1-only; V2 LRU-evicts finished children), fix rounds can always resume the implementer via followup_task, role files attach to spawns via agent_type on isolated forks (0.145+), full-history forks accept model/reasoning_effort overrides (only agent_type refused), and the V2 spawn allowlist is v2 presets only (others hard-error). Fix: rewrite the multi-agent paragraph version-honest (V1 vs V2 labeled).", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-30-codex-efficiency-fixes-design.md", "source_location": "## The five treatments / ### T3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_30_codex_efficiency_fixes_design_t4_brainstorming_three_path_router", "label": "T4: Brainstorming three-path router (variant C)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The current HARD-GATE text pushes a bounded task to FULL ceremony 5/5, while Z-null (no guidance) and a three-path router both differentiate 5/5: absolute wording suppresses discrimination the model draws natively. The measured waste is the unconditional two-document artifact ritual (spec file -> plan file), not the approval gate. Variant C scales the ARTIFACT across spike/bounded/architectural paths while every path keeps human approval before implementation; guards: classification said out loud, heavier path when in doubt, one-way ratchet, Red Flags against classification-as-escape-hatch. Graded in three layers: adversarial micro, codex ceremony battery, and global regression battery on Claude Code/Gemini.", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-30-codex-efficiency-fixes-design.md", "source_location": "## The five treatments / ### T4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_30_codex_efficiency_fixes_design_t5_explicit_model_child_spawns", "label": "T5: Explicit model on child-issued spawns", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Root spawns are 100% explicit-model at CLI 0.146 (dev 14/14), but the live gap is depth-2: 2/2 child-issued spawns omitted model. Source recon: model without reasoning_effort resets effort to the MODEL's default, not the parent's. Fix: every spawn sets model AND reasoning_effort, plus machine-level backstop via [agents].default_subagent_model / default_subagent_reasoning_effort in ~/.codex/config.toml. Pre-registered caveat: if T1 eliminates depth-2 spawns entirely, T5 grades as root-spawn regression (hold 100%) plus doc correctness and is recorded inconclusive-by-zero at depth-2.", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-30-codex-efficiency-fixes-design.md", "source_location": "## The five treatments / ### T5", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_30_codex_efficiency_fixes_design", "target": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_07_30_codex_efficiency_fixes", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-30-codex-efficiency-fixes-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_30_codex_efficiency_fixes_design", "target": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_30_codex_efficiency_fixes_design_t1_worker_review_prohibition", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-30-codex-efficiency-fixes-design.md", "source_location": "### T1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_07_30_codex_efficiency_fixes_design", "target": "docs_superpowers_